        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As per <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4260678971\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29475\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29475/hovercard?comment_id=3130491248&amp;comment_type=review_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29475#discussion_r3130491248\">#29475 (comment)</a>, we have decided to update the <code class=\"notranslate\">Reporting-Endpoints</code> data to add data points for the <code class=\"notranslate\">default</code> endpoint, and sub-data points to state when each report type started to be sent to the default endpoint.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have added the structure, but am finding it difficult to complete this work:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>It is hard to find anywhere where the endpoint named <code class=\"notranslate\">default</code> is actually defined.</li>\n<li>It is also hard to find data for the report types being sent to that endpoint. For example, the crash report type was implemented in Chrome in v72 (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6683949661159424\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6683949661159424</a>), but the header itself wasn't implemented until v96 (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5712172409683968\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5712172409683968</a>), so I'm guessing the data point for the crash report type being sent to the default endpoint is 96?</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29539",
            "title": "Add Reporting-Endpoints header data on default endpoints usage",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-27T23:33:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-24T11:31:27.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As a result of <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43799#top\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43799/hovercard\">[WebExtensions] Deprecate runtime.PlatformInfo.nacl_arch</a> #43799, it was identified that a number of the <code class=\"notranslate\">PlatformArch</code> values were missing. This PR adds those values.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">To do</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Confirm values supported in Safari.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Content changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4291536432\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43847\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43847/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43847\">mdn/content#43847</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29512",
            "title": "PlatformArch values support details",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-26T17:23:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-19T18:46:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Extends the linter to replace raw <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;code&gt;</code> tags in descriptions and notes with backticks.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29508",
            "title": "feat(lint): replace code tags in descriptions + notes",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-07T12:50:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-17T22:01:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">As part of my mission to document all the missing Wasm features, I am working on making sure Wasm mutable globals are properly documented. We previously had a <code class=\"notranslate\">webassembly.mutable-globals</code> data point, but this was just describing the overall feature itself, rather than the specific parts of the tech that comprise the feature. And it was only used to show a BCD table on the WebAssembly main landing page — having this many BCD tables on the same page is not a great user experience, so I have decided to start removing them and showing the information elsewhere.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have updated the BCD to get rid of that, and:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add a specific subfeature for the <code class=\"notranslate\">mutable</code> option of the <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Global()</code> constructor.</li>\n<li>Add separate data points for the <code class=\"notranslate\">global</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">global.get</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">global.set</code> Wasm text format instructions. I've put these in an <code class=\"notranslate\">instructions</code> directory, and I could also see us adding further directories for <code class=\"notranslate\">definitions</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">types</code>, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is not ready to merge yet. The main outstanding issues are as follows, which I am hoping <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/eqrion/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/eqrion\">@eqrion</a> and colleagues can weigh in here and advise, as well as the BCD folks:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>I have no idea if the browser support versions are correct. For now, I've just copied the mutable_globals support versions. I'm not really sure how to find all this information (for Wasm instructions in general, not just these few instructions) without it being hugely time-consuming. Any thoughts?</li>\n<li>We need to get agreement on whether this kind of structure is appropriate and will work for Wasm?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29503",
            "title": "Add more accurate/specific BCD for Wasm mutable globals",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-07T16:41:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-17T11:53:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes the linter, adding MDN urls for features that include the <code class=\"notranslate\">@@</code> prefix.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Ensures that <code class=\"notranslate\">@@iterator</code> etc gets an <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn_url</code> automatically.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Triggered via <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4233820489\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29441\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29441/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29441\">#29441</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29454",
            "title": "fix(lint): add MDN urls for features with `@@` prefix",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T14:55:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-10T21:23:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates the <code class=\"notranslate\">update-browser-releases</code> script for Safari, adding a <code class=\"notranslate\">\"preview\"</code> entry for Safari TP corresponding to the latest release in the <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/category/safari-technology-preview/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Safari TP blog</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Rather than guessing the next Safari release version, uses the version \"preview\", which is also used in the data.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29421",
            "title": "feat(update-browser-releases): track Safari TP release",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-07T15:18:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-07T14:42:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1152698?u=5ce323090a48b425ec70128365c96809699959f7&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds partial implementation flags and notes for <code class=\"notranslate\">align-self</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">justify-self</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">place-self</code> for all browsers, when they apply to absolutely positioned elements.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tested this in Safari, Firefox, and Chrome, and discussed with Mozilla engineers <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/dshin-moz/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/dshin-moz\">@dshin-moz</a> and <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/emilio/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/emilio\">@emilio</a>.<br>\nMy understanding is that there's a missing piece in all browsers where you can't just apply the above properties and expect them to work on their own. They also require a non-auto <code class=\"notranslate\">inset</code> value.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test case: <a href=\"https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bug2026174.bmoattachments.org/attachment.cgi?id=9557965</a></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..aGyrRV-wHIpQAr8pIRnPwYpz7G37g0Y-NQ2jrasY4w0\"><img width=\"859\" height=\"685\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/1152698/569104114-395644e2-af61-4110-8ccb-279aa443b933.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..aGyrRV-wHIpQAr8pIRnPwYpz7G37g0Y-NQ2jrasY4w0\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 685px;; aspect-ratio: 859 / 685; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px; display: block\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The red box should be centered in the gray box.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Code:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n  .parent { position: absolute; inset: 20vmin; background: gray; }\n  .child { position: absolute; width: 50%; aspect-ratio: 1; background: red; justify-self: center; }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;parent&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;child&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">style</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n  .<span class=\"pl-c1\">parent</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">position</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> absolute; <span class=\"pl-c1\">inset</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">20<span class=\"pl-smi\">vmin</span></span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">background</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> gray; }\n  .<span class=\"pl-c1\">child</span> { <span class=\"pl-c1\">position</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> absolute; <span class=\"pl-c1\">width</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">50<span class=\"pl-smi\">%</span></span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">aspect-ratio</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>; <span class=\"pl-c1\">background</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> red; <span class=\"pl-c1\">justify-self</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> center; }\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">style</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">class</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">parent</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">class</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">child</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adding <code class=\"notranslate\">inset:0;</code> on the child element makes it work.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not entirely sure I'm reading the spec correctly though, and the placement of auto-inset abspos elements may actually be correct. But, WPT seems to show browser differences in this area at least: <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align/abspos/align-self-static-position-001.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Firefox bug that was filed as a result of my discussion with Mozilla engineers: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2026174</a></li>\n<li>Related Chromium issue: <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/376097648</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29342",
